 "result_text": "`get_schema` should no longer crash when a device like Junos replies without the `ietf-netconf-monitoring` namespace. I haven't run it or any tests, and I didn't test against the Junos response from the gist.\n\nThe change is in `GetSchemaReply._parsing_hook` in `ncclient/operations/retrieve.py`. It still looks for `data` in the monitoring namespace first. If that finds nothing, it tries these in order:\n- the NETCONF base 1.0 namespace;\n- no namespace at all;\n- any namespace (`{*}data`).\n\nIf none of them match, the schema data is set to `None` instead of raising `'NoneType' object has no attribute 'text'`.\n\nI couldn't tell from the issue which of these fallbacks the Junos reply needs. The extra lookups are harmless but may be more than necessary.",
